## Issues

- [ ] `description` is ~552 chars (cap 200) and packs the sync contract
  (parseBrainAide call, byte-faithful propagation, fixed `brain` key,
  null-refusal precondition, exit-code semantics, idempotency, single-mutation-surface
  invariant) into one paragraph. Trim to "the user-typed terminal command
  that propagates `brain.aide` into `.mcp.json` under the fixed key, refusing
  null args."
  Traces to: `description` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `intent` is ~298 words (cap 100) and walks the entire flow: parser
  call, interpolateArgs no-op, key preservation, null-refusal reasoning,
  retired-sentinel post-mortem, idempotency, exclusive mutation surface,
  visible-command-boundary invariant. Most of this is Strategy material.
  Trim to a single ≤100-word north star.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 8 items (cap 4); each is paragraph length and
  encodes exact stderr message templates ("`args[3]` is null — run /aide:brain
  config to fill it"), exact JSON shape commitments, exact exit code mapping
  (0/1/2 with full prose), exact log-line shapes. These are unit-test-territory
  invariants; outcomes should commit to "user sees a useful diagnostic naming
  the offending slot," not to the exact words.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + outcomes-purpose test (exact strings, type signatures, function names) + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 10 paragraph-length items mostly enumerating
  retired regressions (literal sentinel coercion, drift auto-resolution,
  prose-body interpolation, name-branching, args introspection, sync auto-running
  from cli/init, brain.aide auto-creation, args index introspection). Forbidden
  content (retired prior designs, migration history). Compress to 3-4 falsifiable
  failure modes ("sync mutates `.mcp.json` outside a user-typed invocation,"
  "sync silently transforms unwireable input into a wireable launch command").
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Strategy` has 6 paragraph-length decisions; each runs 200+ words.
  Decisions encode the exact stderr message format with all 5 error sub-cases
  written out verbatim, the structural-equality drift comparison shape, the
  exact exit-code 0/1/2 table, the parser-reason-passes-through-verbatim rule.
  All are unit-test-territory or code-comment territory.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` reproduce full terminal session
  transcripts with exact stdout/stderr text, exact JSON output shapes, exact
  npx invocation strings, exact path strings. Cap is 2-3 brief examples.
  Forbidden content (exact strings, file paths).
  Traces to: `## Good examples`, `## Bad examples` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Sibling redundancy with `src/cli/init/.aide` and the project root: the
  `.aide/config/` ownership boundary, the visible-command-boundary invariant,
  the YAML-null-as-unwired-slot signal, the four-state brain status vocabulary,
  and the no-introspection-of-args invariant are all restated verbatim from
