  Traces to: outcomes, Strategy, Bad examples | Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

## Retro

The sync spec is bloated because the strategist treated stderr message text
as a contract requiring spec-level enforcement. The right defense for exact
strings is unit tests asserting the strings against constants in code. The
spec should commit to "user sees a useful diagnostic with the offending
index named" and let a unit test pin the exact words.

The recurring pattern across every brain-related leaf in this tree is the
same: the brain-layer parent (currently the project root) does not exist as
a discrete node, so every leaf carries the brain doctrine it inherits. After
the brain-layer parent is introduced and the root pruned, this spec shrinks
to its actual scope: "sync's mutation contract for `.mcp.json` brain entry."
